lines+=['','Ocean / Waretown is Ocean township in Ocean County. The model does not also add Waretown CDP, overlapping county totals, or Ocean township in Monmouth County. Rumson uses its Census place FIPS; the townships use subdivision FIPS. Each municipality is counted once.','', '## What drives the forecast','', '1. **Observed denominator:** occupied households × owner-occupancy rate. Census income and home values inform the proposed segmentation, but do not directly prove lawn-care demand.','2. **Eligible demand:** multiply owner households by an assumed 60–90% lawn eligibility and 35–65% propensity to hire. These are editable hypotheses. They account approximately for condos, HOA-provided care and households doing the work themselves. Renters, vacant/seasonal homes and commercial customers are excluded. Census estimates are held constant; no population-growth uplift is assumed.','3. **Acquisition:** in each town, target 8% of the remaining never-acquired outsourcing pool at launch, adding two percentage points per year up to 16%. Annual retention is 70–80% in the base. Churned customers do not return to the new-customer pool, preventing an invented second finder fee.','4. **Supply cap:** each town has launch providers, annual net recruitment, and a supply ceiling. One provider supports an assumed 40 year-end households. New customers cannot exceed remaining capacity after retained customers. These are qualified-supply targets, not commitments. Providers shared across towns must have capacity allocated once.','5. **Revenue and payment costs:** retained households have a full service season; new customers have half. Service mix and capture/completion rates determine paid visits. Town price tiers and lot mixes form a joint distribution, preserving their correlation. The per-job fee floor and ACH caps apply before averaging.','6. **Costs:** town CAC starts at $55 / $65 / $80 in 2027 dollars and improves 5% each calendar year. Launch budgets are $10,000–$25,000 and local annual operations $4,000–$10,000, with 3% inflation. Local costs exclude customer media/incentives, separately modeled as CAC, and provider onboarding.','7. **Company staffing:** three paid employees cover the first 1,000 active households; add one per 2,500 additional households, rounding up. Salaries retain the earlier $100,000–$130,000 fully loaded annual assumptions, including founder pay. Corporate overhead starts at $60,000 with 3% annual inflation. Equipment is $5,000 per employee per year. These are capacity-planning assumptions, not approved hires.','', 'The downside reduces assumed outsourcing by 20%, acquisition rates by 40%, and supply targets by 20%, while increasing cash CAC by 35%. The upside raises outsourcing 15% (capped at 100%), acquisition rates 50%, and supply targets 25%, and lowers cash CAC 20%. Existing case retention, service frequency, payment mix and completion assumptions still apply. No income-based retention uplift is assumed.','', '## Revised base results','', '| Metric | 2027 | 2030 | 2033 |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
